<h1>Capabilities</h1>
<p>DemiEngine is alpha/beta. This page is the honest support matrix — do not infer production support from an example alone.</p>

<h2>Stable</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Versioned JSON projects, scenes, prefabs, HUD trees, assets, data, and saves</li>
  <li>Lua lifecycle scripts, explicit service imports, editor property annotations, events, timers, hot reload, modular LuaLS stubs</li>
  <li>Contextual input actions for keyboard, mouse, gamepads, touch, gestures, and virtual controls; deterministic input replay</li>
  <li>2D rendering: sprites, cameras, animation, tilemaps, materials, startup-loaded game shaders, particles, masks, nine-slice, debug overlays</li>
  <li>Box2D physics: multiple collider shapes, contacts, queries, joints, CCD, kinematic movement, matching debug drawing</li>
  <li>2D navigation and reusable controllers</li>
  <li>Retained tree UI: anchors, layout containers, focus/navigation, themes, localization, UI prefabs, text editing, virtualization, accessibility snapshots</li>
  <li>Schema-backed immutable game data</li>
  <li>Audio mixing, buses, snapshots, scheduling, streaming, spatial voices, entity-attached sources</li>
  <li>Deterministic asset importing, dependency validation, portable <code>.demipack</code> archives, locked <code>.demipkg</code> packages, cooking</li>
  <li>Linux cooking/packaging and runtime bundles</li>
  <li>Profiling, CSV reports, deterministic replay, headless smoke tests, capability gates</li>
  <li>Shared component metadata driving serialization and Inspector</li>
</ul>

<h2>Experimental</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Lightweight 3D: glTF models and skeletal clips, Vulkan GPU skinning with CPU fallback, instancing, culling, model/visual animation LOD, crowd probes</li>
  <li>Jolt rigid bodies, compound colliders, spatial queries, character movement, collider assets, collider generation from models</li>
  <li>Component-based fracture authoring and native Blast/Jolt impacts, masonry, proximity activation, debris cleanup, destruction checkpoints</li>
  <li>Mesh denting, height-map surface relief, textured materials, local and directional lights, tone-mapped panorama skies, mipmaps, particles, post effects</li>
  <li>Native editor with scene/HUD/prefab stages, hierarchy, Inspector, Undo/Redo, embedded Play, asset folders, diagnostics, profiling</li>
  <li>Host-authoritative networking with contracts, ownership, late-join state, reconnect primitives, dedicated server</li>
  <li>Async HTTP/HTTPS with verified TLS</li>
  <li>Android APK/AAB build and signing (feature and device qualification stays scoped)</li>
  <li>Video and cutscene playback on media-enabled builds</li>
  <li>Production text/dynamic UI and the 3D animation adapter</li>
</ul>
<div class="docs-note"><strong>Not delivered yet</strong><p>HDR, metallic/roughness PBR, environment reflections, and local reflection probes are roadmap work, not current rendering features.</p></div>

<h2>Planned</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Android cooking integration</li>
  <li>Professional desktop 3D expansion (HDR/PBR/reflections, large-world workflows, structural stress)</li>
  <li>Broader production qualification across devices</li>
</ul>

