<h2>Compatibility policy</h2>
<ul>
  <li>During alpha/beta, breaking changes are allowed without deprecation. Examples, templates, packages, schemas, stubs, tests, and docs migrate in the same change.</li>
  <li>Breaking changes keep one current way to do each job; examples, templates, packages, schemas, stubs, tests, and docs migrate with the change.</li>
  <li>Every durable document keeps <code>format_version</code>. Unsupported versions are rejected with clear diagnostics.</li>
  <li>Unknown components are errors unless registered extensions own them.</li>
  <li>Saves are never silently deleted; incompatible saves keep clear diagnostics and migrations where possible.</li>
  <li>Compatibility guarantees begin with the first explicitly designated production release.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Measure, do not assume</h2>
<p>Benchmark reports record specific runs (hardware, resolution, build configuration, workload). They do not establish a general capacity guarantee for every scene or device. Use <code>demi run --profiler</code> and the qualification examples for comparable numbers.</p>